p.src:
In lecture units $T=1/\beta$, so $-\frac{\partial}{\partial\beta}
 =
 T^2\frac{\partial}{\partial T}.$ At fixed volume define the heat capacity of the whole sample by $C_V\equiv
 \left(\frac{\partial\langle E\rangle}{\partial T}\right)_V.$ Equation [eq:sm5-energy-variance-beta] becomes $\boxed{(\Delta E)^2=T^2C_V}
 \qquad (k_B=1).$ For laboratory temperature $T_K$, where $\beta=(k_BT_K)^{-1}$, $\boxed{(\Delta E)^2=k_BT_K^2C_V}.$

